  "worked_solution": "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=0.\n$$",
